100% agreement. I've been playing Nethack for about 6 years now (or at
least Hack followed by Nethack) and I've never made it to the end. I still
enjoy the game as much now as I did way back when I started. I play at least
once a week sometimes more if the bug is bad, but I engage in little (if any)
nethack abuse. I don't restore from save files (no matter how far the 
character went), I dont examine the source, I don't polypile. I think
robbing shops are fair game, although I almost always get it wrong and
get done for it.

If you play the game in the spirit in which it was created (i.e. you're an
adventurer - go adventuring. Be not afraid of monsters - attack til your
last hit point) the game will always be difficult and enjoyable.

I did make it to hell once - but the character was so good that he became
boring to play - so I wipied him. I think that if I ever did make it to 
the end I probably wouldn't want to play it any longer, so maybe I
really don't want to make it to the end and that reflects in my style
of play - but at least I enjoy it!!

